WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.267
This is how people celebrate

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.203
the Lunar New Year in Daly Village.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.208
This year's celebration

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:10.143
is particularly special.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.745
The adults around this table

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.747
all work in factories in the cities.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.815
This is the only time

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.118
when many of them can see their children,

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.656
China's zero COVID policy over the last

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.192
three years has made it all even harder.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:38.038
The people here are warm and inviting

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:38.738
people here.

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:39.372
They're so friendly.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.840
I was just walking by and they're like,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.575
Come join us for lunch.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.377
We came to this place in China,

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.579
Southern Guedes O Province to help.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:47.814
A part of rural China

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.649
is celebrating the Lunar New Year

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.118
without pandemic restrictions.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.219
This village is nestled

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.521
deep within the mountains.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.056
Its remote hard to access

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:56.856
because of that.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:57.957
For hundreds of years

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.060
since the villagers have settled here,

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:00.960
the majority of the food

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.462
they eat, they either grow

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.130
or they raise themselves.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.899
We visited villagers home.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.470
Sanjaya greets us with a treat

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.571
and alcohol,

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.705
both made from rice

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:15.975
from the paddy fields nearby gourmet

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.610
drinking is a big part

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.946
of celebrating here. Not go

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.283
and Sanjay is popular in this village.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.319
The door is barely closed.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.988
Relatives stream in to use this machine.

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:29.989
The poor

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.158
and the freshly baked sticky rice.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.360
It turns into paste.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.362
Her machine is a novelty here.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.698
Before they had to pound the rice by hand

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:41.167
with sticks for hours,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.136
About 1000 people live in this village.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.238
And for hundreds of years, they've lived

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.340
in these traditional wooden houses.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.343
And you can hear the chickens crowing

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:53.413
and there are these ducks as well

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.281
that they raise for food.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.082
In many ways,

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:58.218
this place is like a time capsule.

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:59.686
Its physical isolation

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.354
has preserved their way of life

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.856
for centuries.

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.924
Through China's dong ethnic minority.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.459
They have their own language,

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.194
tradition and culture,

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.362
but they can't escape

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.731
the economic realities of modernity.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:12.966
Normally,

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.734
this village is full of the elderly

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:15.735
and young kids

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.004
with most of the working age adults gone,

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:20.206
working in faraway factories,

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.608
sending money home.

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.610
It's only for these few days

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.911
during the Lunar New Year holiday

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.280
when they can really all be together.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.149
We came across this migrant worker

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.416
who's just returned from

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.684
Jiangxi province,

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.820
more than 600 miles away.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.155
This is a job, he told me.

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:36.389
He's brought some oranges

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.158
and candies for his son

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.093
and traveled for more than a day to

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.127
get home by bus.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.296
This couple works in

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:43.897
a factory

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:46.533
500 miles away in Guangdong Province,

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.601
making circuit boards

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.082
Wow.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.356
hate when the parents are away,

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.525
their grandparents take care of the kids.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.527
This is common in rural China.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.840
for the first time in three years,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.909
millions of Chinese migrant families

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.612
are finally able to reunite without

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.280
the fear of COVID lockdowns.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:36.482
I try

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:37.183
to find out if

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.518
this village's remoteness

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.385
has shielded it

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.087
in any way from the country's

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:44.190
sweeping wave of COVID cases and deaths.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:45.692
It's all Asia.

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:46.593
Almost everyone

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.227
I speak to on

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.695
camera says no, one around

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.396
them has gotten COVID

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.731
like this elderly woman

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.700
who makes traditional crafts.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.387
But we run into another group

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.389
of young people who say otherwise.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:17.690
The man in the brown

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.858
jacket with his back

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.893
turned is a doctor at a hospital

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.028
in a nearby city.

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:47.954
So we've got the

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:50.890
three government minders following us.

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:52.458
A group of six government

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:53.526
minders greeted us

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.561
the moment we arrived in the village.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.230
It's common for local officials

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.331
to keep a close eye

00:04:58.331 --> 00:04:59.432
on foreign journalists

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:01.567
in their jurisdictions,

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.903
especially persistent in this village,

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.005
following our every move.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.273
So we just wrapped up the interview

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:08.308
and one of the government

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:11.544
minders is sitting out over there

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:13.212
and immediately.

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:14.314
At least four of them

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.816
booked rooms in our same hotel or nearby.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.785
So we drive out of the village

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:19.218
to visit

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.253
a public hospital

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:21.387
in a neighboring county

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.222
about 2 hours away,

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.857
hoping these government minders

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:25.925
won't follow us

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.527
so people will feel more comfortable

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:29.395
speaking freely.

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.431
We walk inside the fever clinic.

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:34.300
It's almost entirely empty.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:35.001
In the main

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:36.969
hospital area, there are more people,

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.504
but it's not packed.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.473
It's a stark contrast to the images

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:41.374
of overflowing

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:42.875
hospitals in major cities

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:45.411
across China for weeks before

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.212
I ask a nurse

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:47.847
on another floor of the hospital

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.082
if it was packed with patients

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.283
a few weeks ago.

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:52.318
She says it's always packed

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:53.619
and busy here.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:56.089
We try to ask why it looks empty here.

00:05:56.089 --> 00:05:57.056
But another doctor

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:59.125
interrupts, ending our interview.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:00.693
We find one woman,

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:01.894
a patient's family member,

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.996
who is willing to speak to us

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:21.981
Soon after we realized

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:23.015
we're being followed,

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:25.518
apparently by a whole different crew,

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:26.719
there's at least two

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:27.920
or three government minders.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.021
They are still following us

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:29.622
all the way here.

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:31.391
It's very obvious

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.025
they follow us to hospital

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:35.161
after hospital, preventing anyone

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:36.596
from speaking to us.

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:38.097
I try confronting them,

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:46.873
Are you thinking, Karl, now

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:48.474
he's walking away.

00:06:58.151 --> 00:06:59.552
And what happens next?

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:01.521
During my interview, with this girl

00:07:01.521 --> 00:07:02.455
shocks us.

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:11.931
Okay, so I interviewing the girl,

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:14.066
and then the minders literally

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.135
took her away from us.

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:17.203
The man pushes the girl

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:18.337
and her family away,

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:20.072
then later leaves them alone.

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:20.940
But her interviews

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.176
in the marketplace are over.

00:07:23.176 --> 00:07:25.678
China's CDC says the COVID peak across

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:27.146
the country has passed.

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:30.082
But in rural areas like this, experts say

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:32.752
there's likely far more silent suffering

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:34.620
people who died at home

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.521
because they couldn't

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.323
afford to go to the hospital

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:39.725
or were unable to get there on time.

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:40.026
Back in

00:07:40.026 --> 00:07:41.227
the village were greeted

00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:43.262
by the sound of squealing pigs

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.398
getting ready to be slaughtered.

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:47.366
It's a Lunar New Year tradition.

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:48.301
Some of the families

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:49.802
raised the pigs themselves.

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:51.137
Others buy them from sellers

00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:52.038
like this woman,

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:52.872
who tells me that

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:54.207
now that people can gather

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:55.441
and barbecue together.

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:57.076
Her business is booming.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.212
Decades ago for

00:07:59.212 --> 00:08:01.013
most countryside families.

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:02.615
This was the only time of the year

00:08:02.615 --> 00:08:04.550
when they could afford to eat meat.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.185
Now talk about bringing the family

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:07.487
together to feast.

00:08:07.487 --> 00:08:10.022
So this is a whole family of relatives

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:10.890
are all getting together

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:11.924
for the Lunar New Year,

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:14.160
enjoying that freshly killed pigmeat.

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:15.661
Sanjaya teaches me

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:17.230
how they dress and do their hair

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:18.631
for special occasions,

00:08:18.631 --> 00:08:19.198
showing me

00:08:19.198 --> 00:08:21.133
all the clothes and fabric in her home

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:23.469
that she's made herself sewing.

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:25.571
Just a thin strip of this cloth

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:27.673
takes her more than a day.

00:08:39.619 --> 00:08:40.386
But the mothers here

00:08:40.386 --> 00:08:42.088
tell me they don't expect their kids

00:08:42.088 --> 00:08:43.956
to carry on all of the traditions.

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:44.657
One of Sandy's

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:46.025
relatives, a young woman

00:08:46.025 --> 00:08:47.827
who works at a cosmetics factory

00:08:47.827 --> 00:08:49.862
600 miles away in Guangdong,

00:08:50.129 --> 00:08:51.330
invites us to her home

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.283
Her parents and grandparents are proud

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:11.918
she sends most of her earnings

00:09:11.918 --> 00:09:13.052
back to them,

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:14.186
whether it's in the village

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:16.088
or in faraway factories.

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:18.224
They're hardworking people.

00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:19.525
They'll do whatever it takes

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:21.527
to give their kids a better life,

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:24.263
even if it means long about separation

00:09:24.263 --> 00:09:25.231
from them.

00:09:25.231 --> 00:09:27.133
Making reunions like these

00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:28.601
all the more meaningful.

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:31.971
Selina Wang, Daily Village.

00:09:31.971 --> 00:09:32.939
Guedes in China

